  "title": "Karnataka Cabinet Clears 5% Park Land for Public Infrastructure",
  "summary": "The Karnataka Cabinet cleared a Bill to amend the Government Parks (Preservation) Act, 1975, allowing up to 5% of park and garden lands to be alienated for public infrastructure and utility projects, following opposition from the BJP on environmental grounds. The amendment aims to support the proposed 17-km tunnel road project connecting Hebbal and Central Silk Board.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Karnataka Cabinet approved a Bill to amend the Government Parks (Preservation) Act, 1975, allowing up to 5% of park and garden land to be alienated for public purposes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The amendment allows the sale, lease, gift, exchange, or mortgage of up to 5% of park and garden lands for public infrastructure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The amendment is significant in the context of the proposed 17-km tunnel road project.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
